SUMMARY:[現場] BOOK LAUNCH: Literature and Emergency Law in Kashmir and N
 orthern Ireland
LOCATION:Building 80\, Auditorium
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/book-launch-literature-and-emergency-
 law-in-kashmir-and-northern-ireland
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/book-launch-literature-and-em
 ergency-law-in-kashmir-and-northern-ireland\n報名/票券: https://docs.g
 oogle.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdQah3_uTR1wJVo42_g9NlrI24aytDewDVEZUSI91E2EPRH
 xg/viewform\n\nThe Department of African and African American Studies (DAA
 AS) in collaboration with the Center for South Asia (CSA) cordially invite
  the Stanford Community for a special book launch!\n\nWe are excited to ce
 lebrate the publication of a new book by our visiting postdoctoral scholar
 \, Danny Shanhan\, Ph.D titled\, Literature and Emergency Law in Kashmir a
 nd Northern Ireland.\n\nThis book is the first substantial study of emerge
 ncy law's relationship to literature in either the Northern Irish or the K
 ashmiri conflict and develops an original legal history that links these l
 aws to a shared British colonial root. Engaging a wide range of fiction\, 
 poetry and film\, from canonical poets Seamus Heaney and Agha Shahid Ali t
 o contemporary works by Anna Burns\, Mirza Waheed\, and Bollywood filmmake
 r Vishal Bhardwaj\, the book examines the literary response to the suspens
 ion of normative legal rights such as habeas corpus\, the right to silence
  and even\, in Kashmir\, the right to life. By bringing these literary cul
 tures together for the first time\, it develops a literary and legal histo
 ry that reveals common roots in colonial-era jurisprudence. The book re-si
 tuates these corpora\, often isolated in scholarly work\, as important par
 ts of the global\, material legacies of colonialism.\n\nJoin us for an eve
 ning of conversation\, community and celebration and Danny shares his work
 . This will be followed by a discussion and Q&A with Roanne Kantor\, Assis
 tant Professor of English.\n\nRefreshments will be provided.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
